Here is the root cause:
The dev_map_redirect_multi() function used hlist_for_each_entry_safe() for iterating hash buckets in the DEVMAP_HASH branch, which runs under RCU protection (softirq context) but the iteration does not use rcu_dereference(), lacking the necessary memory barrier and RCU lockdep validation. This can cause data races on weakly-ordered architectures and fails to pair with RCU writers. Additionally, dev_map_enqueue_multi() had an incorrect lockdep condition (lockdep_is_held(&dtab->index_lock)) instead of rcu_read_lock_bh_held(), leading to potential false positives in lockdep validation.

